+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+Every registered tool declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is forwarded to the model, and `ToolRegistry.execute` enforces that schema before calling the tool's executor. A call whose input fails validation resolves to a `ToolResponse` describing the failure rather than throwing or invoking the executor, so the model can read what was wrong and correct the call on the next tool round instead of ending the turn with a transport error.
+
+## Validation contract
+
+- `execute` validates `input` against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before calling the executor; on failure it returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` describes the failure, and the executor is never invoked ([validated by: returns a ToolResponse naming the missing required field and does not invoke the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L6)).
+- A wrong-typed field is rejected with a message naming the field path and the expected type; the offending value does not appear in the rejection text or in any log line produced during the call ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field naming the field path and expected type while omitting the offending value from the result and logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L29)).
+- Validation enforces `required`, declared types, and `enum` only; it does not inject `additionalProperties: false`, coerce types, or apply defaults, so valid input carrying an unlisted extra property is passed through to the executor unchanged.
+- `execute` throws `Unknown tool: <name>` only when no tool is registered under `name`; every call to a registered tool whose input fails schema validation resolves to a `ToolResponse` so `ChatOrchestrator.processMessage` can feed the rejection text back to the provider on the next round within the `maxToolRounds` budget.
+
+## Schema compilation
+
+- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time; an uncompilable schema causes `register` to throw synchronously with a message that names the tool, so a broken schema fails at startup rather than mid-conversation ([validated by: throws at register time when the inputSchema is uncompilable and names the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L74)).
+- A static tool's schema is compiled once at registration rather than recompiled on each `execute` call, while a function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves per call and validates against the schema current at that call, cached by the resolved schema object.
